WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.190
Film Courage: How do you train someone to
believe that their success is inevitable?

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:08.531
Erica Wernick, Author/Success Coach: I drill
it in them a hundred times until we believe

00:00:08.531 --> 00:00:09.550
it.

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:14.910
I think that whenever you're trying to take
on a new belief sometimes our subconscious

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:23.010
mind needs proof and so I try to tell people
what that means in tangible terms like why

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:29.789
is your success inevitable and what will happen
if you don't believe your success is inevitable,

00:00:29.789 --> 00:00:30.789
right?

00:00:30.789 --> 00:00:37.790
If you don't believe your success is inevitable
it is very likely that you have a plan b that

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:42.860
you have some sort of backup plan that you
have set up a timeline for yourself where

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:46.480
if this doesn't happen in five years I'm going
move back home or I'm going to do something

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.220
else, right?

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:52.650
You're coming up with insurance because you
don't believe 100% (it's like a prenup for

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:58.150
your dream) because you don't believe 100%
that it's going to work out and what happens

00:00:58.150 --> 00:01:04.850
is that when you don't believe your success
is inevitable you don't take the big risks

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:09.090
you don't put yourself out there in the same
way because you don't believe that it can

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:16.670
happen right so it really impacts the strategy
or the actions that you end up taking so I

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:24.119
try to help people by showing them where you
know where their current belief of not believing

00:01:24.119 --> 00:01:28.740
their success is inevitable is leading them
and how that's playing out and I like to inspire

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:34.799
people to show them like why I think their
success is inevitable and I think that if

00:01:34.799 --> 00:01:40.859
you can take away the lottery feel of succeeding
right because I think that you'll hear often

00:01:40.859 --> 00:01:46.060
oh succeeding in Hollywood that's like winning
the lottery so for example one of my clients

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:50.060
I think this is in my book she said that that
was something that she had heard a lot you

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:55.209
know that good luck trying to make it in Hollywood
that's like winning the lottery and so I said

00:01:55.209 --> 00:02:00.840
to her can you count on your hand can you
name any people you know who have won the

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:05.770
lottery and she was like you know I don't
think I know anyone who's won the lottery

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:14.209
I said okay now can you count on your hand
and name me people who have succeeded in Hollywood

00:02:14.209 --> 00:02:19.200
and she listed like 10 people that she personally
knew who were doing well in the industry and

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:25.760
so you know because we want to give our subconscious
brain the subconscious part of our mind some

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:30.010
sort of tangible proof to hold on to and so
when we go through that it's like oh okay

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:35.489
so it's actually not as hard as winning the
lottery it's not that random because I i can

